                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "d8b492db-1dbb-4390-b603-c55ec1a71b93",
                        "entry_id": "0fb68a88-1322-37be-aa6f-a6fdd11563ef",
                        "tags": [
                            "masculine"
                        ],
                        "form": "tsarévitch"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1c6fdc16-5f2e-39e9-9764-771f4415ec25",
                        "entry_id": "0fb68a88-1322-37be-aa6f-a6fdd11563ef",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Princesse héritière du trône de Bulgarie ou de Russie, fille aînée du tsar."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fee3b26c-07ed-4af9-acce-357e3593ef3d",
                                "sense_id": "1c6fdc16-5f2e-39e9-9764-771f4415ec25",
                                "text": "Le serviteur arriva faire connaître cet ordre :\n— Si tu veux te marier à la tsarevna mets sur pieds pour demain tout un régiment.\n— C'est bien ce sera fait mais si après cela le tsar allait se dédire je m'emparerais de tout son royaume et prendrais de force la tsarevna."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ce25b98c-5baa-43b1-a67c-fe7a56fbb1c6",
                                "sense_id": "1c6fdc16-5f2e-39e9-9764-771f4415ec25",
                                "text": "Enfermées dans le terem, gynécée tatar ou byzantin, les tsarines et les tsarevnas laissaient les tsars à la grossièreté de leur sexe. La Moscovie n'eut ni châteaux ni palais ; le Kremlin n'était qu'une forteresse et un couvent, […]."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b88b2dba-f8cc-4376-a040-e03aa9c13e35",
                        "source_entry_id": "0fb68a88-1322-37be-aa6f-a6fdd11563ef",
                        "source_sense_id": "1c6fdc16-5f2e-39e9-9764-771f4415ec25",
                        "target_lang_word": "tsarevna",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "tsarevna",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4db2a1ba-68c6-39e8-94db-bf98174e82b0",
                                        "entry_id": "43f7b018-75c5-385b-aa4d-906248dd0a4b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The daughter of a tsar."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "782072c1-bd5e-4836-9ff5-8dd3c5eabc31",
                                                "sense_id": "4db2a1ba-68c6-39e8-94db-bf98174e82b0",
                                                "text": "The Tsaréviches and Tsarévnas have each separate apartments and servants to look after them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "29844969-81b7-49c5-b1a5-4f60c8a933d8",
                                                "sense_id": "4db2a1ba-68c6-39e8-94db-bf98174e82b0",
                                                "text": "The ban on marriage for the tsarevny was clearly linked with developments in Russia’s political structure and religious status."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3a492cff-4462-4985-b930-4639ed510c26",
                                                "sense_id": "4db2a1ba-68c6-39e8-94db-bf98174e82b0",
                                                "text": "If my research treats the potential of Muscovite tsaritsy and tsarevny to participate in affairs of the realm optimistically, this does not imply that I deny the difficulties of their position."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "520be9fc-3d58-4f8d-ad77-c862774e9f01",
                                                "sense_id": "4db2a1ba-68c6-39e8-94db-bf98174e82b0",
                                                "text": "And a long line of bridegrooms courted the tsarevna one after another:[…]Perhaps the fastidious tsarevna might even have found some of the bridegrooms to her liking."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4cd1622c-9e76-469e-b58b-679f4b2a5cfe",
                                                "sense_id": "4db2a1ba-68c6-39e8-94db-bf98174e82b0",
                                                "text": "There he became acquainted with maids in service to Ekaterina Alekseevna, Peter the Great's half-sister, and through them, he gained the tsarevna’s favor."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9a9ccef5-eac5-4578-a333-82828d39261e",
                                                "sense_id": "4db2a1ba-68c6-39e8-94db-bf98174e82b0",
                                                "text": "And no women were more walled in than the tsarevny, the daughters of the tsars, for they were prohibited from marrying on the grounds that no Russian was high-ranking enough for them and no suitably prestigious royal foreigner professed the true faith, that is, Russian Orthodoxy. So the grandiose ambitions of the tsarevny’s fathers led to lifelong spinsterhood for them."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d74f050f-eb75-49ad-b50d-340a3eb6aec3",
                        "source_entry_id": "0fb68a88-1322-37be-aa6f-a6fdd11563ef",
                        "source_sense_id": "1c6fdc16-5f2e-39e9-9764-771f4415ec25",
